commit 203911ea26f2292a2ba270007e517d3a1fd5c361
Author: Van Tran <940988+vantt@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Thu Sep 3 16:53:17 2026 +0700

    feat(mdview): defer project indexing to background, redirect after login, add folder landing pages
    
    - register/open/mdview_view_file no longer block on a full recursive
      scan: a newly-registered project's row is created empty and a
      detached `mdview refresh` process backfills it, while the requested
      file is still indexed synchronously the moment its URL is opened.
    - Login now returns the visitor to the page that required auth (via a
      short-lived mdv_next cookie) instead of always redirecting to /.
    - A folder with no matching file redirects to its direct README/index.md
      child, same landing convention the project root already used.
    
