Author: Van Tran <940988+vantt@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Sat Sep 5 03:00:26 2026 +0700

    feat(mdview): edit and save markdown in place from the Docs page
    
    An Edit button beside Copy swaps the rendered article for a CodeMirror 6
    editor over the raw source (markdown highlighting, line numbers, undo,
    search, light/dark theme), with a plain textarea as the fallback if the
    bundle fails to load. Save (Ctrl/Cmd+S) PUTs the text to
    /api/projects/:id/files/*path; the daemon writes the file atomically and
    re-indexes it in the same step so title, search, and backlinks update at
    once.
    
    The page ships a hash of the source it rendered and the editor sends it
    back, so a file an agent or another tab changed meanwhile is refused with
    409 and overwriting becomes an explicit second action. Only files already
    in the index are writable. A live-reload event for the file being edited
    is parked while the draft is dirty.
    
    The CodeMirror bundle is vendored (tools/codemirror-bundle builds
    assets/codemirror.min.js), served locally, and fetched only on the first
    Edit click.
    
